      "text": "The believer is spiritually perfected in Christ. Grace permanently removes divine condemnation. Sanctification is the alignment of mind and body with the perfected spirit. Faith aligns the believer with what Christ has already made available. The Holy Spirit produces manifestation. The believer abides by allowing the words of Christ to remain within and form the heart, mind, intentions, and disposition according to His pattern. Grace-manifestation flows from union with Christ and dependence upon the Holy Spirit; it is not the manipulation of spiritual forces. Natural law remains, but divine curse has been removed. Grace never stops flowing. Positional union remains permanent, while experiential participation varies. Divine mystery remains where Scripture does not fully explain."
